From 2d32bffa9733c17bac13e47d2ad101c9404c8da8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Meredith White <meredith.white@tinybird.co>
Date: Mon, 20 Jul 2026 15:48:51 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Serialize p.json() query params as JSON strings

Query params declared with p.json() are typed to accept a structured
object, but query() serialized every non-array value with String(value),
turning { configOverrides: { foo: 1 } } into "[object Object]". The
server's JSON() template function then json.loads() that and fails with
"Error parsing JSON: '[object Object]'".

Serialize plain objects with JSON.stringify. Arrays containing objects
(JSON array params) are serialized as a single JSON string; arrays of
primitives (Array params) keep their per-element append behavior.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
